Subject: [PATCH] CVE-2026-54517: jackson-databind @JsonView bypass for setterless/creator properties
Origin: upstream
 - https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/5bf23edb4221f7dd2ec8e71ff6d26c61640f261d (PR #5969)
 - https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/7dc7a17459e70b7db071cfdf06d2d96d70d4069d (PR #6004)
Bug: https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues/5969
Description:
 In BeanDeserializer._deserializeUsingPropertyBased and several sibling
 property-based-creator paths (record-update, unwrapped, external-type-id) and
 in BuilderBasedDeserializer, the @JsonView active-view filter was not enforced
 on the regular-property buffering branch (and on creator-property branches in
 some sibling paths). Setterless/merging collection properties or other
 view-restricted members could therefore be populated from attacker JSON when
 deserializing under a less-privileged view, bypassing the @JsonView guard.

 This patch adds the missing prop.visibleInView(activeView) (and
 creatorProp.visibleInView(activeView)) checks on every affected branch and
 introduces paired JUnit regression tests covering the setterless, builder,
 record-update, unwrapped POJO and external-type-id paths.
Forwarded: not-needed (already upstream)
Applied-Upstream: 3.1.4

